        // The test assumes c.owner == address(this). If not, calls will revert; that's acceptable.

        // Call sendMoney on c, forwarding value and calldata to target via c. This is the key differentiating call.
        // Use low-level call path in P (which forwards all gas) so the target's fallback can reenter C.fallback and increment depositsCount.
        c.sendMoney(target, sendValue, data);

        uint after = c.depositsCount();
        // On the original P, the low-level call allows the target's fallback (if it calls back into C) to run and increment depositsCount,
        // so after should be strictly greater than before for targets that perform such reentry. The mutant M uses transfer which prevents
        // that reentrancy in typical cases, so the property will be violated by M.
        assert(after > before);
    }

